#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""CARE-Droid v3: bounded dual-prototype evidence with nested early stopping.

The stable ordinary Global24+S7 expert remains the layer-2 backbone.  A local
dual-prototype branch may only add a bounded logit correction:

    final_logit = ordinary_joint_s7_logit + max_delta * tanh(local_delta)

This is an evidence enhancement, not confidence overwrite.  Two variants are
compared under the frozen Global24/A25 protocol:

* DualProto_ES: bounded local evidence, nested early stopping, ordinary BCE;
* DualProto_ES_FixKeep: the same model with higher cost for breaking samples
  that the cross-fitted ordinary Joint-S7 backbone already classifies correctly,
  plus a soft keep-consistency term.

For every 2017 outer fold, the correction-training backbone probabilities are
generated by an additional inner cross-fit.  Epoch selection uses a stratified
holdout inside the outer-training data, then the selected epoch count is refit
on the entire outer-training fold.  All region scalers and prototype statistics
used for final prediction remain training-fold-only.  Future labels are never
used for training, epoch selection, weighting, or threshold selection.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

